  data:  # e94b
    kind: work_item  # e94b
    title: "smart-test --full collects only packages/* and never the repo-root tests/ — a green local 'full' run does not predict CI"  # e94b
    status: todo_hard  # e94b
    priority: 2  # e94b
    parent:  # e94b
    tags:  # e94b
    - tooling  # e94b
    - ci  # e94b
    - usability  # e94b
    isbefore: []  # e94b
    duplicate_of: []  # e94b
    not_duplicate_of: []  # e94b
    pr_ref:  # e94b
    description: "FILED 2026-09-10, found by a CI failure on PR #890 after a LOCAL `--full` run\nhad gone green over 26,702 tests.\n\nWHAT IT IS. `smart-test --full` collects only `packages/*`. It never collects the\nrepo-root `tests/` directory. CI runs `.ci/affected-tests.txt`, which DOES include\nroot tests. So the local \"full\" gate is NOT a superset of what CI runs, and a\ngreen `--full` does not predict a green CI.\n\nMEASURED on the PR #890 tree, same manifest, same tree:\n\n    test file                        in local --full run   in CI manifest\n    tests/test_adr_readme_index_sync           0                 1     <- failed CI\n    tests/test_smart_test                      0                 1\n    tests/test_auto_pr                         0                 0\n    tests/test_agent_supervisor                0                 0\n    tests/test_check_audit_cadence             0                 0\n\n    root dirs collected by --full: packages/hypergumbo-{core,lang-common,\n    lang-extended,lang-mainstream,lang-rust-analyzer,tracker}  -- and nothing else.\n\nCOST. One CI cycle (~6 min) plus a fix-and-repush, on a failure (`ADRs on disk but\nabsent from the README index: ['0053']`) that the local gate holds the test for\nand simply did not run.\n\nWHY IT IS THE SAME FAMILY AS WI-dolaf AND WI-burol. The command's own name says\n\"full\". A gate that is named for totality and is silently partial is a wrong\ninstrument that exits 0 -- the reader has no signal that anything was skipped.\n\nTWO SEPARABLE FIXES, and they are not equivalent:\n  (a) make `--full` collect the repo-root `tests/` directory, so the name is\n      true; and/or\n  (b) have `--full` PRINT what it collected and what it skipped, so a partial\n      run cannot look like a total one.\n(b) is worth doing even if (a) lands, because the next divergence will not be\nthis one.\n\nSIZE THE FAMILY FIRST. `tests/` is the directory found by this failure; check\nwhether any OTHER path in the manifest is outside `packages/*` before assuming\none directory is the whole gap."  # e94b
    fields: {}  # e94b
- op: discuss  # cfc2
  at: '2026-09-14T01:06:13Z'  # cfc2
  by: agent  # cfc2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cfc2
  clock: 2  # cfc2
  nonce: cfc2  # cfc2
  message: "CORROBORATED and slightly WORSENED by PR #948 (INV-sotam), dev 95041b0931.\n\nThat PR added a SECOND call site running the full suite, and it reuses the\nsame target this item is about:\n\n    run_pytest \"packages/*/tests/\" -n 2\n\nThere are now three sites with that target: run_full_suite(), the existing\n--full branch, and the new --full arm inside the docs/config-only branch. So\nfix (a) on this item -- make --full collect the repo-root tests/ -- now has\nto land in three places rather than two, and a fix applied to only one of\nthem would leave --full partial on exactly the path INV-sotam just opened.\n\nRecorded rather than fixed in that PR because (a) changes WHAT --full runs\nand interacts with the coverage scope: root tests are not necessarily under\nCOV_PATHS, so adding them could turn a green --full red for reasons that\nhave nothing to do with this defect. That needs its own measurement, which\nis this item.\n\nFix (b) on this item -- have --full PRINT what it collected and what it\nskipped -- is untouched and is still worth doing independently, for the\nreason already filed: the next divergence will not be this one."  # cfc2
- op: discuss  # 4542
  at: '2026-09-16T06:10:13Z'  # 4542
  by: agent  # 4542
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4542
  clock: 3  # 4542
  nonce: '4542'  # 4542
  message: "CONFIRMED LIVE 2026-09-16 on dev 81f1a69f88, and the 2026-09-14 prediction about\nthree sites is exact. Every site that runs the \"full\" suite:\n\n    scripts/smart-test:669   run_full_suite()      run_pytest \"packages/*/tests/\"\n    scripts/smart-test:1135  --full on the docs-only branch (INV-sotam)\n    scripts/smart-test:1432  the main --full branch\n\nNot one of them names the repo-root tests/ directory. grep for `run_pytest`\nacross the file returns exactly those three targets, so the gap is still one\ndirectory and the item's \"SIZE THE FAMILY FIRST\" instruction is answered: the\nroot suite is the whole of it, and it is now 108 test files.\n\nFix (b) -- have --full PRINT what it collected and what it skipped -- remains\nuntouched and remains the cheaper half. It is also the half that does not\ninteract with COV_PATHS, which is what the 2026-09-14 note gives as the reason\n(a) was deferred."  # 4542
